<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#first-sea-lord">Glossary</a> · Term · office</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Sea Lord</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Sea Lord is the professional head of the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a> and the senior naval officer on the Admiralty Board. Holders have included John Fisher, who led the navy's modernisation before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-louis-of-battenberg">Prince Louis of Battenberg</a>, who resigned in 1914 amid anti-German feeling. The office continues today under the Ministry of Defence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-sea-lord.jpg" alt="First Sea Lord" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TcfkaPanairjdde · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Admiral_-_Royal_Navy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
